s.json loaded first (handlers.ts:66, projects.ts:69, store.ts:82); unrealistic trigger."},{"location":"app/src/main/reader/log.ts:213","claim":"A future line time keeps 'heard' on for the skew plus 15 minutes.","why":"Writer and reader use the same machine clock (scripts/router-app.sh:142; reader/log.ts:213,280); a future line needs a backward clock step while the router is dead, seconds under NTP; a live router's next heartbeat corrects it (scripts/router-worker.sh:19); planned rule (reader/log.ts:12)."},{"location":"app/src/main/watcher/watch.ts:132","claim":"Trailing-only debounce lets a burst defer the read until it ends.","why":"Stated design (watch.ts:2-4), pinned by watch.test.ts:80-91; lag already capped by the minute re-read (watch.ts:90); only ref/HEAD events reset the timer."},{"location":"app/test/integration/watch-view.test.ts:112","claim":"The only real fs.watch test skips in the sandbox and the test note does not declare it.","why":"Declared in the tip's test note integration.covers ('real fs.watch, skipped where the sandbox refuses file events'); the skip fires only when the probe (watch-view.test.ts:20-34) errors or sees nothing in 2 s, and prints its reason; ran here: skipped in 21 ms on EMFILE."},{"location":"app/src/window/fake/fake.ts:85","claim":"The fake's failing scenario fails waiting.get and its view ignores fake project adds/removes.","why":"Failing every request but state.get is the fake's pre-W5 convention (fixtures.ts:13; fake.test.ts:87-95), the real bridge can answer failed for any handler (src/main/bridge.ts:108,124); fixed view documented (fake.ts:6); no window code reads waiting.get yet (hooks.ts:47; contract.ts:167)."}],"nits":[{"location":"app/src/main/handlers.ts:64","finding":"Each view read loads projects.json twice (handlers.ts:66 and :69) plus settings.json; the second projects read is plain redundancy.","waived":"A few small local file reads per debounced read or minute; nothing observable. The fixing session may drop the s